    "title": "'One Shining Moment' video: Watch the 2026 NCAA Tournament montage after Michigan wins national championship | Sporting News",
    "text": "The confetti has fallen in Indianapolis, and March Madness is officially over. Luckily, we have something to help us remember the best moments for the rest of time.The NCAA is releasing its annual \"One Shining Moment\" montage on Monday night, with Luther Vandross' iconic rendition serving as the backdrop for the NCAA Tournament's best moments. Originally written to be played after the Super Bowl, the song has instead been used for college basketball's premier event since 1987. The NCAA Tournament breaks hearts, but it always delivers in one form or another. This year was no exception. From Braylon Mullins' iconic shot and Dylan Darling's buzzer-beater to surprise wins by High Point and Iowa, there are no shortage of moments to remember fondly (or not so fondly, depending on which team you root for) in 2026.Here's the first look at \"One Shining Moment\" after Michigan won the national championship on Monday night.MORE: Explaining the NCAA's annual 'One Shining Moment' video2026 NCAA Tournament 'One Shining Moment' videoOne Shining Moment is here:This year's montage was loaded with memorable moments from a tournament that was filled with them.Braylon Mullins, Dylan Darling, Alvaro Folgueiras, Trey Kaufman-Renn all hit game-winning shots in the final seconds that made appearances, and Otega Oweh's long-range buzzer-beater to force overtime vs. Santa Clara received a few seconds as well. The final moments of High Point's upset over Wisconsin, which included Chase Johnston's first 2-pointer of the season, found their way in, along with Terrance Hill Jr.'s shot to sink North Carolina.\"One Shining Moment\" always shows the dark side of March, so the devastation of players and coaches was featured prominently. That included Tyler Tanner's near-miss at the buzzer against Nebraska.Dan Hurley was featured prominently throughout the video, from his memorable gestures to his meme-able faces. His reaction after Mullins' shot was a particularly fun moment in the montage.As is tradition, the video ended with Ian Eagle's call of the final seconds of Michigan's national championship game win and Dusty May lifting the trophy with his team.MORE: Most March Madness wins by school",
